ost-run judging is batched the same way.\n1592\t- **Four settled matters sit in two groups.** A reader's matter bundled two points, such as \"70% growth guidance, while customer\n1593\t  forecasts indicate a doubling\". Search is therefore counted over pairs (a later member and an earlier member of the same group),\n1594\t  so a matter can belong to two pairs. This mirrors the Step 1 bundling mechanism of the Step 2 log.\n1595\t\n1596\t**Post-run judge prompt.** It gains a neutral `optional` verdict, so that D372's optional entries are not called noise. Noise is\n1597\treported without a line. I settled this wording myself.\n1598\t\n1599\t**Launched** (c8 pins identical in every run folder):\n1600\t- dev ×3 at 08:43, in `poc/data/clean-step1-c8-dev-d{1,2,3}-2026-11-09/`;\n1601\t- the fresh Step 1 run at 08:51, after the lists were frozen, in `poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step1/`.\n1602\t\n1603\t## 43. Acceptance on the fresh set: every line met; links are the weak point (2026-11-09)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c06c24f-8f77-4add-9443-7081a27b7903","uuid":"89b6608f-8b92-4d80-9317-5ce27004bf67","timestamp":"2026-11-09T01:02:52.460Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md","content":"## 42. Acceptance set chosen and readers' lists frozen; runs launched (2026-11-09)\n\n**Fresh set.** 50 news articles from 2026-09-05 to 09-07 that no run has used, old or new (Council B, `council/an-codex.md`: FREEZE\nAND LAUNCH).\n- The procedure is `select_fresh.py`: a census of 10,871 files that refuses unless every dev and test id is found.\n- Inside those days, 8 used items were skipped. The days are a weekend and the US Labor Day holiday, with no NVIDIA posts.\n- Manifest sha256 `81f3f579…`.\n\n**Pre-run readers.**\n\n| Step | Who | Output |\n|---|---|---|\n| First reading | Reader A | 138 matters and 24 repeat groups |\n| First reading | Reader B | 132 matters and 20 repeat groups |\n| Settling | Third reader | 139 settled matters: 128 listed by both readers, 11 kept by the third; 83 core |\n| Settling groups | Third reader | 26 repeat groups (82 members) and 26 dossier details |\n\nAll quotes are exact spans of the source.\n\n- **Every reader matter is accounted for.** Of A's 138, 136 were taken and 2 dropped with reasons. Of B's 132, 125 were taken and 7\n  dropped.\n- **Hand check of two articles.** The year-ahead forecast and the Wistron share sale are plausible, and slightly strict: the forecast\n  article's retold quarter results were left out. The standard keeps an old actual only optionally.\n- Frozen in `poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/SHA256SUMS` (`settled.json` `91caaa0b…`).\n\n**Two process findings:**\n- **A single reader session over all 50 articles stopped after 5.** It returned `status: incomplete`. The third reader was re-run in\n  batches of ten articles, plus one call for the groups. Post-run judging is batched the same way.\n- **Four settled matters sit in two groups.** A reader's matter bundled two points, such as \"70% growth guidance, while customer\n  forecasts indicate a doubling\". Search is therefore counted over pairs (a later member and an earlier member of the same group),\n  so a matter can belong to two pairs. This mirrors the Step 1 bundling mechanism of the Step 2 log.\n\n**Post-run judge prompt.** It gains a neutral `optional` verdict, so that D372's optional entries are not called noise. Noise is\nreported without a line. I settled this wording myself.\n\n**Launched** (c8 pins identical in every run folder):\n- dev ×3 at 08:43, in `poc/data/clean-step1-c8-dev-d{1,2,3}-2026-11-09/`;\n- the fresh Step 1 run at 08:51, after the lists were frozen, in `poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step1/`.\n\n## 43. Acceptance on the fresh set: every line met; links are the weak point (2026-11-09)","numLines":40,"startLine":1564,"totalLines":2289}}}
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/round-1.jsonl:36:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LfnCygWLUSbZ8CA5CqfcuW","type":"tool_result","content":"3:## 0. Frame\n35:## 1. Census on stored runs ($0; `census_unfiled.py`, `poc/data/clean-step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/census-*.json`)\n53:## 2. Mechanism\n91:## 3. Council A (`council/a-*`, `b-*`)\n116:## 4. Arms and probe 1 (predeclared)\n140:## 5. Probe 1 results (`poc/data/clean-step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/probe-r1/`; 192 sends, $2.51)\n168:## 6. Council B (`council/c-*`)\n181:## 7. Decision council (Alex, 2026-11-08: \"跑council决策\")\n217:## 8. Probe 2 results (`probe-r2/`, 96 sends, $1.21; review `probe-r2-review/` with probe 1's 48 control draws re-read blind)\n252:## 9. Reflection council (`council/f-claude.md`, `f-codex.md`, a fresh cold read)\n285:## 10. Calibration and decision council (Alex, 2026-11-08: \"你跑council loop review 然后决定下一步怎么修改\")\n312:## 11. Alex's rulings on the boundary cases (2026-11-08, his replies to these exact questions)\n330:## 12. Decision council on the next modification (`council/h-*`, `i-*`)\n366:## 13. Round closed (`council/j-*`)\n394:## 14. Council decides under Alex's delegation (`council/k-*`)\n429:## 15. Probe 3 results (`probe-r3/`, 96 sends, $1.18; fresh same-day control)\n444:## 16. Alex reframes what a thesis is (2026-11-08)\n472:## 17. Alex decides the shape (2026-11-08)\n486:## 18. Conditions design: passed the design gate (2026-11-08)\n521:## 19. Build for probe 4 (conditions, c1); Alex: no scorer (2026-11-08)\n550:## 20. Probe 4 read (c1 against the same-day k6b control): mixed; three mechanisms traced to c1's own sentences (2026-11-08)\n633:## 21. Reflection council on the whole record (2026-11-08; `council/v-claude.md`, `v-codex.md`, `w-challenge.md`, `w-codex.md`)\n703:## 22. Arm c2: build, audit, motivating sends (2026-11-08; Alex's /goal: run the loop until the line is met)\n761:## 23. Probe 6 read (c2 against the same-day k6b control; 48 sends, $0.67; `probe-r6/`, `probe-r6-merged/`)\n806:## 24. Council B on probe 6, c3 not sent, the whole bench launched, Step 2 changes built (2026-11-08)\n855:## 25. Whole bench: c2 forward over the 115 dev gold articles (one draw; `gold-c2-flash/`)\n908:## 26. Test set, once (c2; `test-c2-flash/`): line missed; the remaining gap is a product decision (2026-11-08)\n961:## 27. Alex decides: keep material statements with no home, link them later (2026-11-08)\n986:## 28. Arm c4: Alex's decision built; the valuation row aligned with his ruling (2026-11-08)\n1029:## 29. Test set, once for c4 (`test-c4-flash/`): the line is met (one draw)\n1060:## 30. The c4 dev run stopped on a cut answer; the runner misread Alex's retry rule; fixed and continued (2026-11-08)\n1087:## 31. Whole bench for c4 (dev, one draw) and later linking checked (2026-11-08)\n1131:## 32. Step 2 re-measured on the c4 records; Jev's criteria aligned with the merge line (2026-11-08)\n1174:## 33. Arm c5: one party's statement per item (2026-11-08)\n1200:## 34. c5 measured; Step 2 lines 1–2 met on its records; c6 narrows the rule and raises the output cap (2026-11-08)\n1250:## 35. c6 measured: Step 2 lines 1–2 met; Step 1 misses only \"no fragments\" by one per set; the question gold is far stricter than the readers (2026-11-08)\n1311:## 36. Alex decides: open only big matters, by the frozen gold's standard (2026-11-08)\n1328:## 37. Arm c7: the opening rule from the standard's closed set (2026-11-08)\n1369:## 38. c7 test, once; question measure baselines (2026-11-08)\n1398:## 39. Alex: \"你这些改动有我你有好好的跑council 再下手\"; retro council on the unreviewed changes (2026-11-08)\n1441:## 40. Council: complete review of the proposed final configuration (2026-11-08; Alex: \"你的goal 需要严格的跑council 来review 和思考再决策\")\n1494:## 41. c8: whole-request audit, check sends, the checks before freezing, and the acceptance set (2026-11-08/09)\n1564:## 42. Acceptance set chosen and readers' lists frozen; runs launched (2026-11-09)\n1603:## 43. Acceptance on the fresh set: every line met; links are the weak point (2026-11-09)\n1645:## 44. Dev ×3, the reflection council, and the link recheck (2026-11-09)\n1696:## 45. Alex adopts c8 (D387); the PRD carries it; next, the account of weak links (2026-11-09)\n1721:## 46. Cause of link clutter: the model's own account; council stops a send (2026-11-09)\n1750:## 47. Alex approves the link-check design; reflection council on the day; code review and cleanup for check-in (2026-11-09)\n1822:## 48. Commit; the Ohio-guarantee miss diagnosed; one mechanism under two classes (2026-11-09)\n1863:## 49. Arm c9 (the \"covers\" split) probed and stopped (2026-11-09)\n1901:## 50. The failed c9 answers read against the source ($0; Alex: \"先把失败的回答对照原文看清\")\n1948:## 51. Arms c10a and c10b (the D388 read-back) probed and stopped (2026-11-09)\n2020:## 52. Arm c11 (a required company-impact field) probed and stopped (2026-11-09)\n2065:## 53. Deep council on the D388 line (c9–c11), on Alex's word \"run council to review deeply\" (2026-11-09)\n2132:## 54. The focused call for D388 probed and stopped (2026-11-09)\n2194:## 55. Focused call, round 2 (two named causes fixed) probed and stopped (2026-11-09)\n2229:## 56. Focused call, round 3 (D389: 5% of annual profit) probed and stopped on one case (2026-11-09)\n2268:## 57. The programme-versus-deal fix: three drafts blocked; the boundary goes to Alex (2026-11-09)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c06c24f-8f77-4add-9443-7081a27b7903","uuid":"e5302c6d-e8a4-4a93-a5b3-5e47d81dfe96","timestamp":"2026-11-09T00:55:15.783Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"3:## 0. Frame\n35:## 1. Census on stored runs ($0; `census_unfiled.py`, `poc/data/clean-step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/census-*.json`)\n53:## 2. Mechanism\n91:## 3. Council A (`council/a-*`, `b-*`)\n116:## 4. Arms and probe 1 (predeclared)\n140:## 5. Probe 1 results (`poc/data/clean-step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/probe-r1/`; 192 sends, $2.51)\