is adopted. An isolated low-versus-medium reasoning comparison on six known prepared articles completed and was reviewed with setting labels hidden. Both settings stated an example model as actually used in all three article-28 answers. In article 29, stock-market flows were blurred into infrastructure spending in 3/3 low and 0/3 medium answers, but the medium answers did not retain that stock-flow statement. Other attribution and context concerns remained. These are selected-case observations, not a production acceptance or proof of cause. See the [full results](STEP1-REASONING-FIDELITY-RESULTS.md) and [36-answer replay](../poc/data/clean-step1-reasoning-fidelity-2026-11-07/review.html). The [source-fidelity prompt audit](STEP1-FIDELITY-PROMPT-AUDIT.md) maps observed failures to the complete request and signed standards. The council and an independent reader reviewed a field-local wording hypothesis that asks summaries to preserve source qualifications. In a six-article isolated comparison, all three answers in each arm still described an example model as part of the proposed system without preserving the “such as” qualification; other context and linking concerns remained. The field-description candidate is not adopted. [Full results](STEP1-SUMMARY-FIDELITY-RESULTS.md) and [36-answer replay](../poc/data/clean-step1-summary-fidelity-2026-11-07/review.html) preserve the cases and limits; the council is investigating the next step.
